    <item>
      <title>Ferrocene heteroconjugation enables charge transport in DNA monolayers</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79212-2</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Communications, Published online: 11 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79212-2"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41467-026-79212-2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;DNA is a promising self-assembling material for molecular electronics, but efficient charge injection remains challenging because of its deep HOMO energy level. Here, the authors develop a chemically defined DNA–ferrocene conjugate through covalent modification of a DNA duplex and demonstrate an enhanced electrical response. The resulting metal–DNA molecular junctions show how electronic functionality can be programmed by molecular design, providing a platform for quantitative comparison with theoretical models.</content:encoded>
      <dc:title>Ferrocene heteroconjugation enables charge transport in DNA monolayers</dc:title>
